title ALES146 — Lotus's stereo_voiced: the voiced/unvoiced/silent classifier carried into stereo, the suite's second STEREO ANALYSIS rung, one shared band/floor/split and two independent verdicts
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think REMEMBER's living-card edge names Season D consensus arcs, yet the true git nib is deep in Season C (Lotus, ALES145). The recur turn's actual bench is the ALES stereo carry — one mono DSP primitive lifted into stereo per signed round. Crux-first, the next member in ascending mono-ALES order after ALES93 (zero_cross → ALES145) is ALES94 voiced — the classifier that FUSES two analysis readers into one verdict. It is the analysis rung that stands directly on the one just carried, so it is both the ascending-order next and the Lindy-first crux: the analysis corner grows from two readers (level, activity) to their fusion.
think ALES94 classify reads energy (ALES13 RMS) and crossing rate (ALES93 count through the ALES92 band) over one span and fuses them by one rule, energy gate FIRST: rms < floor → silent; else crossings ≥ split → unvoiced; else voiced. Its own crux is that it invents no new measurement — its verdict equals a by-hand decision from the two readers, so it can never drift from them.
think Carried into stereo the plain way (mirroring the stereo meter ALES17 and the stereo zero-cross ALES145): run ALES94's proven mono classify on each channel with ONE shared band, floor, and split, returning StereoVerdict{left,right}. Unlike ALES145's counter the classifier carries NO running state — a verdict is a pure function of one span — so this rung offers ONE form (classify_stereo, the pair) rather than a carried counter, mirroring the meter's whole-master measure_stereo. Validated ONCE up front (schmitt.precheck for band+span, floor vs meter.sample_peak_max) before either channel is read, so a refusal never classifies one channel and returns a half answer; ClassifyError reused whole.
think Proved four laws: the stereo fusion law against ALES94's own classify per channel across four floors and three splits; the read-only/balance law (source byte-for-byte unchanged on both, pair balanced); the independent-verdict law (loud-periodic left over quiet right → voiced/silent, identical master → equal verdicts, energy gate first per channel so a quiet many-crossing channel reads silent not unvoiced); and the atomicity/degenerate law (shared BadFloor/BadThreshold/BadRange refusing before either channel is classified with the clip untouched, the floor-zero convention voiced on both, the span discipline reading only [start,count)).
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, read-only software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo ANALYSIS corner now holds three members: level (ALES17 meter), activity (ALES145 zero-cross), and their fusion into character (ALES146 voiced). The honest lesson: a stateless analysis rung's stereo lift is simpler than a stateful one's — no carried form, just the pair-returning shape of the meter — yet keeps the same one-shared-validation, read-only-of-source discipline. Fusion composes cleanly: the stereo classifier drifts from nothing because the mono classifier it runs per channel drifts from nothing. Witness GREEN (four laws), tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0. Third lap sent this recur turn (ALES144-146), all crux-first continuations of the comparator/analysis class into stereo.
loom witness=ales_stereo_voiced_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=stereo-analysis read=read-only form=pair-returning fusion=energy+crossing crux=fusion-rule-cannot-drift cases=stereo-fusion(4floors*3splits)+read-only+loud-vs-quiet+identical-equal+energy-gate-first+atomicity(floor,band,range)+floor-zero+span-discipline
